# cozy-house - literal colours to rewrite inside NoMansSky's Kvantum SVG.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# Kvantum's [GeneralColors] (kvconfig, derived by lib/derive.py) covers flat
# colour ROLES - button face, text, highlight.color, etc. It does NOT reach a
# colour baked directly into the theme's SVG artwork, and Kvantum draws
# everything - shapes, gradients, strokes - from one SVG per theme.
#
# Measured: Dolphin's Places sidebar kept a GNOME/Breeze blue selection
# (#62a0ea) no matter what Colors:Selection or highlight.color were set to -
# even a wild kdeglobals test value (magenta) changed the focus ring
# elsewhere in the window but never touched the sidebar. Traced to a
# <rect stroke="#62a0ea"> baked into the "button-toggled" element group in
# NoMansSky.svg - not the "#ff00ff" placeholder Kvantum's own runtime tinting
# looks for, just a literal.
#
# FORMAT: same as gtk-recolor.map - "<source-hex>  <palette-colour-name>",
# case-insensitive, right-hand side must be an @define-color name defined in
# palette.css.

62A0EA  theme_selected_bg_color   # button-toggled element - Dolphin Places
                                   # sidebar selection, and anything else
                                   # Kvantum draws via that same shape

# The other half of the SAME gradient - fourteen <linearGradient> wrappers
# all xlink:href a single shared pair of stops, #3584e4 -> #62a0ea. Mapping
# only the light stop above left a visible two-tone brown-to-blue gradient
# on the selection, since a fill:url(#...) is not caught by a plain hex scan
# of the element that USES the gradient, only of the <stop> that defines it.
3584E4  accent_dark_color         # dark stop of the same gradient
